  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>About the Calculator</h2>
    <p>It is a learning and convenience tool. Results come from standard JavaScript arithmetic running on your device, and while the functions are tested, no calculator can promise a perfect result for every possible input. Treat an unusual-looking answer as a prompt to check rather than a verdict.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Rounding Is Normal</h2>
    <p>Computers store most decimals approximately. A long chain of operations can end a fraction of a unit away from the exact value, which is a property of binary floating point rather than a fault in this page. Where a question demands exactness, work in fractions.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Not Professional Advice</h2>
    <p>Nothing here is financial, legal, medical or engineering advice. A number produced by this page has no professional standing and should never be the only basis for a decision that carries risk.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>The Written Guides</h2>
    <p>The guides explain school-level mathematics in plain language and are deliberately simplified in places. They support a textbook and a teacher; they do not replace either, and they do not follow any single exam board's syllabus.</p>
  </section>
